# An order passes four stages, and each has one owner
<callout icon="🧭" color="green_bg">
	An order goes from staff to the list, to the kitchen, to the desk. A late order stops at the list.
</callout>
## The stages
![Four stages left to right on a wide screen, top to bottom on a narrow one, each with its owner. Order (staff), List (Sam), Kitchen (caterer), Desk (Sam).](stills/how-figure-stages.png)
**Each of the four stages has one owner, so a late order has one person to ask.**
## Who a late order reaches
![A grid of order time against menu day. On time on any day reaches the caterer; late on a normal day reaches Sam; late on a menu-change day reaches nobody.](stills/how-figure-matrix.png)
**Only a late order on a menu-change day reaches nobody.**
## One late order, step by step
![A stepper over one late order. Its still frame shows the refusal at the list.](stills/how-figure-stepper.png)
**An order placed at 10:40 is refused at the list, before the caterer sees it.**
## Today's timings
<table header-row="true">
<tr><td>Stage</td><td>Owner</td><td>Closes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Order</td><td>Staff</td><td>10:30</td></tr>
<tr><td>List</td><td>Sam</td><td>10:30</td></tr>
<tr><td>Kitchen</td><td>Caterer</td><td>11:15</td></tr>
</table>
**The list closes with the orders, so nothing waits between them.**
